Z||000070||BBBAD GT||04-19-2001||11:31 PM||||Sorry guys, I won't be making it up this weekend.  A local guy wants to see the Fiero, and I have some family things I have to take care of. Hopefully I'll see all of you at Bob's place in May, if I still have the Fiero.<P><P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero/V8sig.jpg">        <P><A HREF="http://home.att.net/~nomercy5.0/V8Specs.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8 For Sale</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
Z||000071||Archie||04-19-2001||11:46 PM||||Officially the Seminar begins at 1:00 and typically Jim Hallman (our respected NIFE leader and one of my personal heros)tries to get me to limit my seminar to like 90 minutes. But, with all the fun we have, it can last longer. Then many people hangout visiting and looking at cars until well after dark. I usually arrive by 9 AM and I expect people will start arriving well before the 1:00 starting time.<P>This year we will have something new. If you arrive early or stay late, you will have a chance to take a ride in a V-8 Fiero. I will have 3 or 4 of my cars there and several of my customers will have their cars there and we will have several "Designated Drivers" available to take you for a test ride.<P>Everyone is invited, you don't have to be a member of NIFE or any other club to participate.<BR>                     <BR>For the last several years this event has started the NIFE Fiero Events season. This year will be no exception. A couple of years ago NIFE became the first Fiero Club to raffle off a Fiero. This event, again, will be the kick off event, the Raffle car will be here and the ticket sales will begin at this event (car to be given away at the NIFE Fierorama). These tickets always sell out fast & are usually sold out long before the Fierorama, so get them now.<P>Another tradition is the "Burnouts". No, we don't do burnouts with all those people gathered around. Early in the morning, before we set up the chairs for the seminar, I usually lay down several sets of stripes in the shop. For some reason, people who attend like walking thru the rubber chunks I leave on the floor. We practiced that today to determine which car would be laying down the decorations. My Finale won the honors with my "T" top car 2nd & the F-40 close behind.<P>All this and free sandwiches and pop..... be there or be square.<P>Archie<p>[This message has been edited by Archie (edited 04-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000072||Tina||04-20-2001||12:17 AM||||Aaaahhh,.....screamed Tina's V-8.<BR>Whole body shop full of parts,and I can't find nothing to wear to Archie's.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1315468&a=12269353&p=46889000">  <BR>Tina   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P> <p>[This message has been edited by Tina (edited 04-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000073||Oreif||04-20-2001||12:28 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tina:<BR><B>Considering my Fiero doesn'nt have anything to wear.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>I guess, I can't come<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1315468&a=12269353&p=46889000">  <BR>Tina   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>AAAAHHH! Naked Fiero! Aren't you suppose to put up a warning prior to showing such nakedness?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Alas, I won't be able to make it. (Son's B-day party, lot's of people coming over)<BR>I was there last year, Excellent time!<P>Archie, An NIFE member asked if I could relay a message to you, He would like to purchase a Catalytic Converter from you. His name is Rich. He'll talk to you at the meeting.<BR>||||reg||1
